A||||6||DJRice||drip, drip, drip on my floorboard...not antifreeze||||5||
Z||000000||DJRice||08-08-2000||11:23 AM||||Well, I have water on my passenger side floorboard, but its not a leaking heater core.  I believe the water may be running along a housing or something until it ends up in the general area of the heater core.  I suspect, since it didnt rain yesterday when I noticed the drip, that condensation from the AC system may be the culprit, but I cant seem to find where it is entering.  Has anyone dealt with this???<P><P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||5
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||08-08-2000||11:48 AM||||DJRice,<P>   Does your Fiero have a sunroof?  I've parted out one where it looked like a combination of a bad window seal and sunroof caused water to run down along the A-piller and under the floorboard area under the dash causing it to rust out.<P>  I know you said that it hadn't rained, but check the seals, maybe the water didn't run down from under the roof until you drove around or it just took a while for it to soak into the carpet.  Hope this might help...<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||08-08-2000||01:24 PM||||If you think it may be the condensation from the AC, then there may be blockage in the drain. High humidity this time of year produces LOTS of water. I believe that the drain is in the front compartment. I took the fan motor out of my car to check for debris that causes fires (see earlier post) and could see that the housing has a place for water to drain into a plastic "tray" along the wall under the drier (big shiny tank. Taking out the fan motor will allow checking inside of the ductwork and see if there is water inside there. This doesn't seem to happen often in Fieros.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||08-08-2000||02:33 PM||||Unfortunately, I dont have a sunroof, but I think that 286 may be on to something.  I will check to see if my drain is plugged...its probably a good idea to check for critter nests as well given recent discussions.<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||08-08-2000||02:59 PM||||Yep np, think 286 has got it, that's uncommon but it does happen.  Hehe, don't let the little hamster that runs your blower fan squirrel cage get away!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||08-08-2000||04:49 PM||||I had the same problem, and it was the AC condensor water backing up into the car.  The problem was a clogged drain tube.  I got under the front of the car and found the tube only to discover a cob web had been made in it, which was causing the plug.  I was able to get it out with a screw driver and that fixed the problem.  Check the drain.  Oh, and its almost impossible to see it from inside without removing the heater core so I would recommend going from underneath first.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||08-08-2000||04:56 PM||||I have been hunting for that drain tube on my Formula for awhile now, where exactly is it?||||reg||1
